  "reasoning": "The patient presents with red spots all over the body that are itchy, accompanied by fever, headache, and exhaustion. Comparing these symptoms to the reference cases, multiple examples align precisely with this presentation: references describing 'little red spots all over my body' combined with exhaustion and severe headache, as well as those noting 'red, itchy bumps all over my body' with fever and headache, are all diagnosed as chicken pox. While dengue can also feature red spots and headaches, it is characteristically associated with extreme body pain and vomiting, which are absent here. Fungal infections typically present with patches of varying skin colors and lumps/pimples rather than a generalized itchy rash with systemic flu-like symptoms. Therefore, the clinical picture strongly and specifically points to chicken pox.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]chicken pox[/DIAGNOSIS]"
